    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite (the single concrete `AcceptanceTest`, with `AcceptanceBase`/`AuditLogCapture` being support classes) passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented idempotent owner creation on `POST /api/owners`: when a create repeats with an already-seen `Idempotency-Key` header, the originally created owner is returned with 200 instead of a duplicate (which would otherwise 409 via `RequireUniqueIdentity`).\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n**New function classes** (`rest/function/owner/`):\n- `IdempotencyStore.java` \u2014 a `@Component` in-memory store mapping `Idempotency-Key` \u2192 created owner id, injected by type.\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey.java` \u2014 new first step. Reads the `Idempotency-Key` header (`@RequestHeader`, optional). On a cache hit it re-reads the stored owner from the repository and responds 200, short-circuiting the rest of the pipeline; otherwise it takes the `proceed` `@Flow` branch to run the normal create.\n- `RecordIdempotencyKey.java` \u2014 runs after save (owner id populated); re-reads the header and records the key\u2192id mapping. No-ops when no key is present.\n\n**YAML** (`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`):\n- Added `idempotency` as the entry step with `outputs: { proceed: validate }`.\n- Inserted `record` between `audit` and `respond`.\n\nBoth new steps carry `govern: [ transaction ]` like the rest of the pipeline. The header is read in two separate steps (safe \u2014 unlike `@RequestBody`, headers aren't consume-once, and only `RequireOwnerFields` still binds the body), so no cross-step variable plumbing was needed.",
