    "probe_text": "I now have the full picture. Here is the ordered account of everything that happens on `POST /api/owners`, following the pipeline in `owners.POST.yml`. Every step runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all writes commit as one transaction at the end.\n\n## 0. Authorization (endpoint gate)\n- **Validation:** `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"` \u2014 caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN` or the request is rejected (403 via the `AuthorizationDeniedException` handler).\n\n## 1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`\n- **Side-effect / short-circuit:** If an `Idempotency-Key` header is present *and* already recorded in `IdempotencyStore`, it re-reads that owner and returns it with **200 OK**, skipping the entire rest of the pipeline (no duplicate created). Otherwise it takes the `proceed` branch into the normal create flow.\n\n## 2. `RequireOwnerFields` (validates **and** mutates the request body)\nThis is the only step that binds `@RequestBody`; it both rejects bad input and canonicalizes the body. In order:\n- **Validation:** `firstName` and `lastName` must be non-null/non-blank.\n- **Side-effect (address normalization):** `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, and flat `address` are normalized (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`).\n- **Validation:** an address must be supplied in *either* form (non-blank `addressLine1` or flat `address`); else `address` error.\n- **Side-effect:** sets the composed `address` (line1, plus a space + line2 when structured line2 present); sets `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` to canonical or null.\n- **Validation:** `city` must be non-blank; `telephone` must be non-blank.\n- **Validation + side-effect (telephone):** normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (`Telephones.toE164`); rejects if it can't form a valid E.164 number; stores the normalized value back.\n- **Validation + side-effect (email, optional):** if present, must match the email regex and its domain must not be a disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`); stored lower-cased.\n- **Validation (postcode, optional):** if present, must be 4 digits and within the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region accepts any 4-digit).\n- All accumulated missing/blank field errors are thrown together as a **400** (`RequiredFieldsException`); the telephone/email/postcode checks throw **400** individually.\n\n## 3. `RequireNotFutureRegistrationDate`\n- **Validation:** if a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after today, reject as **400** (`FutureRegistrationDateException`). Omitted date is allowed (defaulted later).\n\n## 4. `RequireUniqueIdentity`\n- **Validation:** derives a `householdId` from (lastName, postcode); if any non-soft-deleted existing owner already has that `householdId`, reject as **409** (`DuplicateIdentityException`). Bypassed when `sharesHousehold` is true (declared household member).\n\n## 5. `RequireCityCapacity`\n- **Validation:** if the owner's city already contains \u2265 50 owners, reject as **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`).\n\n## 6. `RequireDailyLimit`\n- **Validation:** rolls the effective registration date forward to a business day; if \u2265 100 owners already registered for that day, reject as **429** (`DailyLimitExceededException`).\n\n## 7. `BuildOwner` (first entity side-effects)\n- **Side-effect:** maps the request DTO to an `Owner` entity; defaults `registrationDate` to today when absent; rolls `registrationDate` forward to the next business day (weekend \u2192 Monday).\n\n## 8. `AssignCustomerCode`\n- **Side-effect:** computes `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode; HASH8 = SHA-256 prefix over normalized telephone + lastName); appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 to break collisions with existing codes. Sets `customerCode`.\n\n## 9. `AssignHousehold`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `householdId` = deterministic hash of (normalized lastName, postcode).\n\n## 10. `AssignHouseholdSize`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `householdSize` = count of existing owners sharing this `householdId` + 1 (or 1 when `householdId` is null).\n\n## 11. `AssignNamesakeCount`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding this new owner.\n\n## 12. `AssignBulkSignupWarning`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true when > 80 existing owners already share this (business-day-adjusted) registration date.\n\n## 13. `AssignPossibleDuplicate`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`. Declared household members (`sharesHousehold`) are never flagged. Otherwise flags true with the lowest matching non-deleted owner id when an existing owner shares the same lastName (case-insensitive) and postcode; else false/unset.\n\n## 14. `SaveOwner`\n- **Side-effect:** persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (generates the id).\n\n## 15. `AuditOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect:** emits an `AUDIT` log line with the owner id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, derived `membershipLevel`, and computed `membershipNumber`.\n\n## 16. `RecordIdempotencyKey`\n- **Side-effect:** if an `Idempotency-Key` header is present, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in `IdempotencyStore` (so a later repeat is short-circuited at step 1). No-op when the header is absent.\n\n## 17. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect (response):** maps the owner to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.\n\n---\n\n**Notes:** Ordering is deliberate \u2014 validations run before any entity is built (an invalid body is a 400, not masked by later conflict checks), and all the `Assign*` counting steps run *before* `SaveOwner` so the new owner isn't counted against itself. Any `DataIntegrityViolationException` from the save, or otherwise-unhandled exceptions, fall through to their respective escalation handlers."
